<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dungan people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dungans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dungans are Chinese-speaking Muslims; the name is used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> for the Hui people of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. After the failure of the great Muslim revolt against Qing rule of 1862–1877, many fled into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, where their descendants live in Kyrgyzstan and Kazakhstan and speak a Chinese dialect written in Cyrillic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dungan-people.jpg" alt="Dungan people" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Professor Hai Feng, Xinjiang University · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dungan-Girls.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
